  - The emergence of autonomous multi-agent systems has revealed a critical infrastructure deficit: while individual agents can execute complex tasks within isolated silos, the ecosystem lacks a standardized mechanism for these entities to discover one another and delegate work across organizational or technological boundaries. [Source: ev-1]
